{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430788-nurad-thaumaturgy-and-third-edition","id":1430788,"title":"Nurad, Thaumaturgy, and Third Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-02T13:50:12-08:00","id":1430788,"title":"Nurad, Thaumaturgy, and Third Edition","content":"I was just reading CoCD: Autochthonia and I got to the chapter on Nurad. Up to that point, only a few bits about Estasian Militat bioenhancements didn't convert well to 3rd Ed., but Nurad has a lot of its background tied to thaumaturgy, including recreating rice from a single grain and creating ironfruit. With thaumaturgy changed from something that everyone can learn to do to something only a few in a thousand can do and not something that can be researched, that seems like a major problem to converting the setting.<br /> <br /> Any ideas how to bridge this setting element?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T14:02:09-08:00","id":1430790,"title":"","content":"I've been running a campaign that revolves around Nuradi characters exploring Creation, so I've put some thought into this, and my solution was simply that Nurad still did a bunch of that stuff, thaumaturgy just wasn't involved. A lot of it can be explained by using the mundane Abilities, simply backed up by the advanced technology of Autochthonia. When a mortal technician is working in a biogenesis laboratory that's a municipal charm made of green jade, she can do more things than the same person working with primitive clay beakers and an iron cauldron in some run-down tower in Creation. And the more impressive stuff is adequately explained by sorcerous workings. Mortals can be sorcerers, after all, and the Sodalities in particular, I feel, all have their own secret techniques to initiate those who have the right gifts and aptitude into the power of sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T14:29:10-08:00","id":1430792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430788-nurad-thaumaturgy-and-third-edition?p=1430790#post1430790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been running a campaign that revolves around Nuradi characters exploring Creation, so I've put some thought into this, and my solution was simply that Nurad still did a bunch of that stuff, thaumaturgy just wasn't involved. A lot of it can be explained by using the mundane Abilities, simply backed up by the advanced technology of Autochthonia. When a mortal technician is working in a biogenesis laboratory that's a municipal charm made of green jade, she can do more things than the same person working with primitive clay beakers and an iron cauldron in some run-down tower in Creation. And the more impressive stuff is adequately explained by sorcerous workings. Mortals can be sorcerers, after all, and the Sodalities in particular, I feel, all have their own secret techniques to initiate those who have the right gifts and aptitude into the power of sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with your analysis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T16:09:07-08:00","id":1430800,"title":"","content":"<i>Was</i> Genesis Arts even a reference to thaumaturgy in the first place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T16:14:02-08:00","id":1430803,"title":"","content":"Minor sorcerous workings with lots of assistants would definitely be an alternative in portraying those too i'd imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T18:27:16-08:00","id":1430816,"title":"","content":"Remember that one cult of thaumaturgic necromancers who achieved a false immortality by moving their lower souls into their soulgems, or something?<br /> <br /> They unwittingly made liches of themselves like Puella Magical Girls, and their secret society hadn't lasted long enough for the consequences to become apparent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T19:25:10-08:00","id":1430819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430788-nurad-thaumaturgy-and-third-edition?p=1430800#post1430800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Was</i> Genesis Arts even a reference to thaumaturgy in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a bunch of references to more than just Craft (Genesis), like cybernetic prosthetics, that were accomplished via thaumaturgy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T19:38:19-08:00","id":1430820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430788-nurad-thaumaturgy-and-third-edition#post1430788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just reading CoCD: Autochthonia and I got to the chapter on Nurad. Up to that point, only a few bits about Estasian Militat bioenhancements didn't convert well to 3rd Ed., but Nurad has a lot of its background tied to thaumaturgy, including recreating rice from a single grain and creating ironfruit. With thaumaturgy changed from something that everyone can learn to do to something only a few in a thousand can do and not something that can be researched, that seems like a major problem to converting the setting.<br /> <br /> Any ideas how to bridge this setting element?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unique prodigies in Nurad, use of some municple Charms that the cities had whicha llowed htem to allow Soldates something akin to sorcerous workings without being sorcerers, and simply something that looks like actual Earth cloning via some form of technobable. None of it need to be categorically what we consider the same thing as other stuff. It's only a problem if you consider thaumaturgy like, a natural category of stuff basically.<br /> <br /> Hell, ironfruit being thaumaturgy in 2e is actually to me it just mission-creep. Seriously, standard long term breeding practices in an exotic environment do fine. We got edible corn without it being magic afterall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T03:19:40-08:00","id":1430856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430788-nurad-thaumaturgy-and-third-edition?p=1430820#post1430820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unique prodigies in Nurad, use of some municple Charms that the cities had whicha llowed htem to allow Soldates something akin to sorcerous workings without being sorcerers, and simply something that looks like actual Earth cloning via some form of technobable. None of it need to be categorically what we consider the same thing as other stuff. It's only a problem if you consider thaumaturgy like, a natural category of stuff basically.<br /> <br /> Hell, ironfruit being thaumaturgy in 2e is actually to me it just mission-creep. Seriously, standard long term breeding practices in an exotic environment do fine. We got edible corn without it being magic afterall.</div> </div> </div> </div>What\u2019s mission-creep?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T04:13:41-08:00","id":1430858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430788-nurad-thaumaturgy-and-third-edition?p=1430856#post1430856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s mission-creep?</div> </div> </div> </div>The slow expansion of an operation beyond its initial mission statement. In this case, expanding thaumaturgy rules to model steampunk science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T05:54:41-08:00","id":1430862,"title":"","content":"Thank you. That actually sounds kinda cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T10:28:57-08:00","id":1430887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430788-nurad-thaumaturgy-and-third-edition?p=1430862#post1430862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you. That actually sounds kinda cool.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The problem with the way it was done in 2e was that thaumaturgy ended up eating up a <i>lot </i>of the territories of other Abilities. Thaumaturgy was tied to your Occult Ability, which meant that if you wanted to make soap, create a bandage that stopped bleeding automatically, or breed an animal with unusually good traits, all of which were examples of thaumaturgic rituals, you had to have dots in Occult. I much prefer the approach I suggested above, which is that Abilities already include the capacity to do various impressive things within their purviews, given the right tools and knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T14:20:27-08:00","id":1430914,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't really like the idea of straight up sorcery as the method of achieving these things in Autochthonia, because the image of the personalities involved doesn't really fit.<br /> <br /> I still don't quite but the idea that Nurad's presented achievements were portrayed as a result of thaumaturgy, but in the end that doesn't really matter. The question is whether those things were there because they were naturally emergent from thaumaturgy, or if thaumaturgy was used as the convenient gameplay mechanism for how these particular qualities of the big gaslamp fantasy world were achieved.<br /> <br /> I feel as though the setting as a whole is always one that has carried the implications that at the higher levels of functioning, quite a bit of the everyday wonders end up accessible to normal people in creation and use. Precisely how that works gets to be a bit of an open question because it's not relevant to the time period played in, and it gets to be a mystery of the First Age. Nurad could get a similar benefit when all of this is supposed to be stuff that happened a long time ago, they took a big hit for, and have hard turned away from.<br /> <br /> Besides, regular Creation still has some forms of folk magic, some of which are apparently going to get some description in Across the Eight Directions.<br /> <br /> And like, with the correct Craft you can mix guano and red jade together to make firedust. I think there can be something similar for that in the world where the tools and knowledge might be more sophisticated and accessible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T05:47:04-08:00","id":1430978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430788-nurad-thaumaturgy-and-third-edition#post1430788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any ideas how to bridge this setting element?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly depends on how different you think Autochthonia is from Creation beyond the aesthetics. <br /> <br /> It's pretty viable to treat that world as a giant industrial-looking cave inhabited by spirits that resemble robots and other forms of artificial intelligence, in which case most of the technology that's not provided by Alchemical municipal charms is a result of successfully requesting the aid of the AI spirits or tapping into whatever underlying systems they're part of. In some ways that represents a fairly realistic take on technology because very few people with expertise in a particular field could recreate their tools from scratch if they found themselves on another world without them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T16:38:34-08:00","id":1431095,"title":"","content":"See, this is something that I overlooked. I remember that the Solar Terrestrial Circle Sorcery Initiation charm also lets you learn any Thaumaturgy you come.<br /> I have been running that as &quot;any Sorcerer can learn Thaumaturgy&quot;, which I now know is wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T17:45:04-08:00","id":1431102,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I've long questioned the necessity of Artifact crafting being a thing that requires Essence manipulation considering the barrier to entry presented by the Ability requirements and the difficulty of accumulating the necessary successes without Charms. The function of the Sodalities in particular is one where it kind of recognises the need for a wider base of people to be capable of doing so and justifying how becomes more convoluted than it needs to be.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, why do more people know how to do this stuff in Autochthonia than they do in Creation?&quot; Maybe about the same reason as more people can programme computers now than there were in the 50s.<br /> <br /> Although I suppose that there's still a matter that cybernetic limbs are probably custom jobs performed by specialists in every event event, and the actual initial event of turning one grain of rice into many consumes more resources than using that to start implementing regular crops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T17:46:26-08:00","id":1431103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430788-nurad-thaumaturgy-and-third-edition?p=1431095#post1431095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, this is something that I overlooked. I remember that the Solar Terrestrial Circle Sorcery Initiation charm also lets you learn any Thaumaturgy you come.<br /> I have been running that as &quot;any Sorcerer can learn Thaumaturgy&quot;, which I now know is wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, as per &quot;On sorcerers and thaumaturges&quot; section on page 490. Chosen who unlock sorcery automatically gain the Thaumaturgist merit <i>but</i> mortal sorcerers do not. <br /> <br /> This is quite easily overlooked as this is not <i>mentioned</i> in any of Terrestrial Circle Sorcery charms, but <i>only</i> in the Thaumaturgist merit itself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T20:01:25-08:00","id":1431113,"title":"","content":"I also like the idea that some of the magic-science things that Demiurges and whoever perform in Autochthonia are as much or more a function of a Metropolis' municipal super-science laboratory campus Charm as of the mortals who work in it.<br /> <br /> Mortal sorcerors seem like something that should be an enormous deal in Autochthonia, because individuals aren't SUPPOSED to have that kind of power except when granted by God and State.<br /> <br /> That kind of personal power seems too liberating for the setting, and thus more appropriate for the mutants of the elemental far-reaches or the Void cultists and their Apostate Champions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T13:13:53-08:00","id":1431314,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with Sunder the Gold on not having mortal sorcerers running around the Octet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T17:02:13-08:00","id":1431338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430788-nurad-thaumaturgy-and-third-edition?p=1431314#post1431314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to agree with Sunder the Gold on not having mortal sorcerers running around the Octet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that even Alchemicals, if they want to become sorcerors, have to accept a permanent dot of Clarity that will never go away because they cannot uninstall the Sorcery Charm.<br /> <br /> By design or convenient accident, Clarity is one of many ways that Autochthon and Autochthonia constrains the freedom of Alchemical Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, it would fit the setting's oppression if any mortal who self-initiates into sorcery -- purposely or accidentally -- would be declared some kind of dangerous Void mutant by the state, and hunted to death by its mortal, Exalted, and spiritual enforcers.<br /> <br /> This serves to drive more sorcerors into the arms of the polar mutants and Void cultists, of course, which ends up creating self-fulfilling prophecies and making the enemies of orthodoxy more powerful and unorthodox.*<br /> <br /> Very Warhammer 40K-ish.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Except for the Crystal mutants? I think those might be socially acceptable to Autochthon's souls?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-06-2021, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T18:12:06-08:00","id":1431342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430788-nurad-thaumaturgy-and-third-edition?p=1431113#post1431113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mortal sorcerors seem like something that should be an enormous deal in Autochthonia, because individuals aren't SUPPOSED to have that kind of power except when granted by God and State.<br /> <br /> That kind of personal power seems too liberating for the setting, and thus more appropriate for the mutants of the elemental far-reaches or the Void cultists and their Apostate Champions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, now I'm thinking about how this is the kind of argument I might have made against mortal sorcerers in the Realm, until compelling scenarios were put into publication for the Immaculate Order having provisions for incorporating them. The institutions of Autochthonia's state seem at least as strong, if not even firmer.<br /> <br /> I'd be restrained mostly by a sense that it doesn't quite sit easily in their caste system, and that I'd still want the proposal of changing an individual's caste after the fact to still be extremely unique.<br /> <br /> Althooouugghh... the Populat still has a few specialist duties that fall just under the remit of Sodalities. I don't think it would be totally out of place for a member of that caste to not get nearly the same resources or academia as members of the Tripartite (whose applications for sorcery seem fairly obvious) and often be assigned to high value and high risk operations in the Reaches (that also conveniently place them far from home).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-07T11:12:08-08:00","id":1431409,"title":"","content":"It also seems like something that could help people further distinguish the Eight Nations from each other. I notice that even after Compass: Autochthonia we're still prone to talking about the Octet like it's a monoculture. For example, Estasia's Half-Souled Amulets apparently originate from &quot;gremlin-derived technology&quot; which would be unthinkable if we were thinking about this in such general terms, so there's scope to be ideologically flexible here.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 01-09-2021, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-07T12:01:05-08:00","id":1431412,"title":"","content":"Both good ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-07T23:49:17-08:00","id":1431449,"title":"","content":"I'd also note that the system you use doesn't mean you use the the same justification. For example, using the sorcerous workings rules, doesn't mean that you define the people using it in Authocthonia as sorcerers. It's just a way to work on thins without having to create an entirely new rules system.<br /> <br /> So, you could define it as something that say, requires a workshop for any circle (because this is being used as ritual/magitech), and has hard limits based on the support of your nation/alchemical. <br /> <br /> And then, you have a much smaller (perhaps only alchemical) number of individual who are <i>real</i> sorcerers, complete with magic. But as far as Autocthonia is concerned, they're two different things. Populat Sam is just part of a factory that refines various metals using the techniques the resonate with the Maker. That scary, scary Regulator can cat the same kind of magic as the Champions can, without needing a factory or anything like that.<br /> He just has to explain <i>absoluely every use</i> of that power to his superiors. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T09:26:17-08:00","id":1431471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430788-nurad-thaumaturgy-and-third-edition?p=1431449#post1431449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also note that the system you use doesn't mean you use the the same justification. For example, using the sorcerous workings rules, doesn't mean that you define the people using it in Authocthonia as sorcerers. It's just a way to work on thins without having to create an entirely new rules system.<br /> <br /> So, you could define it as something that say, requires a workshop for any circle (because this is being used as ritual/magitech), and has hard limits based on the support of your nation/alchemical.<br /> <br /> And then, you have a much smaller (perhaps only alchemical) number of individual who are <i>real</i> sorcerers, complete with magic. But as far as Autocthonia is concerned, they're two different things. Populat Sam is just part of a factory that refines various metals using the techniques the resonate with the Maker. That scary, scary Regulator can cat the same kind of magic as the Champions can, without needing a factory or anything like that.<br /> He just has to explain <i>absoluely every use</i> of that power to his superiors.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would only matter if a player is playing Populat Sam. And even if the player was, Populat Sam would not have the authority to decide what he's making, let alone to keep what he makes. So working on a super-magical working or artifact is no ultimately no different for him than producing another couple of cogs.<br /> <br /> If NPCs are making things that someone else orders and uses, then you don't need mechanical rules for that. It's happening entirely in the background.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you are an Alchemical or a member of the ruling elite, and the mortal NPCs are working on your project, and you keep the product, so Populat Sam and his buddies are just part of your crafting process, and probably not even important enough to count as a Means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T10:01:22-08:00","id":1431473,"title":"","content":"Also hinges on what Initiations are most common or known there. If the Initiation is steeped in the same sense of receiving the grace of the Machine God, then no challenges to the state ideology. Then alternate initiations become a story hook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T10:32:45-08:00","id":1431475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430788-nurad-thaumaturgy-and-third-edition?p=1431473#post1431473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also hinges on what Initiations are most common or known there. If the Initiation is steeped in the same sense of receiving the grace of the Machine God, then no challenges to the state ideology. Then alternate initiations become a story hook.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was my logic, yeah. Basically, I think <i>no</i> initiation is really &quot;effortless&quot; - they all either require quite a bit of work and study to get to the point of being able to be initiated, or for the more &quot;luck-based&quot; ones, like Scarred By Dreams and Nightmares, there's an <i>absurdly </i>larger quantity of people who went through much the same experiences, but just came out mad, dead, or both. It's the same in Autochthonia, I think. The Sodalities and the Theomachry have their own specialized initiations, which they put promising members through, and which involve a great deal of specific training and such, and culminate in people being given some kind of &quot;treatment&quot; to awaken their sorcerous power.<br /> <br /> For example, I picture the one that the Conductors use as involving touching a live electrical essence cable to your soulgem, and leaving it there for minutes or hours. If you have the determination to endure the pain and the knack to channel most of the essence away from your vital areas, you survive and get strongly electrical-themed sorcery. If you don't, well, unfortunate. The point is, though, that all these are means of power that are very definitely controlled by the state and its various sub-sections. A Populat member can't access any of the initial training that's absolutely required to be able to channel the essence of that cable in the first place, so trying it just means an agonizing death. And while there might be a kilometer-deep pit of crystal shards that one person, a thousand years ago, came out of with light-themed sorcery after they threw themselves in just as a luminous surge was happening, everyone who's tried it since then has just died horribly, impaled.<br /> <br /> So sorcery doesn't really violate the &quot;power is controlled by the state&quot; conceit of Autochthonia, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T19:55:54-08:00","id":1431529,"title":"","content":"Part of &quot;power is controlled by the state&quot; is that the power can be taken away by the state. Even Alchemicals, without state sanctioned support, lose access to most of their Charms, can't upgrade their Attributes, and are otherwise extremely restricted in what they can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T20:53:54-08:00","id":1431532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430788-nurad-thaumaturgy-and-third-edition?p=1431529#post1431529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of &quot;power is controlled by the state&quot; is that the power can be taken away by the state. Even Alchemicals, without state sanctioned support, lose access to most of their Charms, can't upgrade their Attributes, and are otherwise extremely restricted in what they can do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The same logic applies to the 2e version of thaumaturgy, however. Once someone learns it, they've got it forever, and while they might need ritual accoutrements to perform the ritual, that goes for a bunch of spells too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalt